{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan uses the standard import-based EXTRAS probe (\"s3\": (\"git_remote_s3\", ...)), which is detected via find_spec/import_module in extra_installed()/guard_import(), while simultaneously asserting the package is 'a CLI, not a library' with 'No import of the helper package itself'. If the git-remote-s3 distribution ships only a console script and no importable top-level `git_remote_s3` module, the standard guard would report the extra as MISSING even when the helper CLI is present on PATH.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3fc3db3c933d8510","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach steps 2–3; AC line 'exposes require_s3_helper() and a \"s3\" EXTRAS probe'","norm_id":"n3b6550268d26bb45","priority":0.1452,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.55,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Cite a verifiable source (git-remote-s3 upstream changelog / release notes / the acquire_lock commit) pinning the exact version at which IfNoneMatch='*' per-ref locking landed, or route the 0.3.2-lock claim to a short SPIKE, rather than resting the MIN_GIT_REMOTE_S3 floor on a self-attested session experiment.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a live experiment this session verified git-remote-s3 0.3.2 carries that lock (its acquire_lock uses IfNoneMatch=\"*\" with a TTL steal)'","resolve_symbol('git_remote_s3') and resolve_symbol('git-remote-s3') both returned UNRESOLVED — the version-specific lock behavior cannot be confirmed from the repo or tools (EVIDENCE CLASS: Unverified/Partially-verified)","T3 severity rule: an asserted-but-unverified external capability the plan depends on = MAJOR"],"finding":"The load-bearing external-capability claim — that git-remote-s3 0.3.2 carries the IfNoneMatch='*' per-ref lock in acquire_lock, which fixes MIN_GIT_REMOTE_S3='0.3.2' as the floor — is grounded only in a self-attested 'live experiment this session' with no verifiable upstream citation. If the lock was actually introduced in a later version, the >=0.3.2 floor admits a lock-less client and the epic's core anti-corruption guarantee is defeated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fecead811e168f003","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context/Problem paragraph; Approach step 3 (MIN_GIT_REMOTE_S3 = \"0.3.2\")","norm_id":"n6a065e9c77bc39e0","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["The IfNoneMatch per-ref lock was introduced in a version above 0.3.2, so >=0.3.2 passes a client without the lock and multiple-bundles corruption still occurs despite the guard reporting 'success'."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.65,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes",