' but does not deprecate/steer consumers away from require_extra('s3') for readiness"],"finding":"The `s3` EXTRAS import-probe (used by extra_installed/require_extra/guard_import) and require_s3_helper() measure different things and can disagree: find_spec('git_remote_s3') can succeed while the git-remote-s3 console script is absent from PATH (or the reverse — script present, dist version metadata missing). The plan does not state which is the authoritative readiness signal for S3 preflight consumers, so a downstream child could call the weaker require_extra('s3') and believe it proves the helper is exec-ready and >=0.3.2.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc768540a8621abae","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach steps 2-3 / Rationale paragraph","norm_id":"nd894bb9ba1dade80","priority":0.2063,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["A preflight/doctor child calls require_extra('s3') (or extra_installed) for readiness and passes even though git-remote-s3 is not on PATH — git then fails opaquely at push time, defeating the guard's purpose","git_remote_s3 importable but console script shadowed/absent in the operator's PATH"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","rever